1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,848
A wireless board needs more than a

2
00:00:01,700 --> 00:00:02,407
box.

3
00:00:03,084 --> 00:00:05,659
This Raspberry Pi Pico 2 W case

4
00:00:05,511 --> 00:00:07,564
is designed with OpenAI Codex.

5
00:00:08,242 --> 00:00:11,047
The FreeCAD work is real, recorded with

6
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:11,751
OBS.

7
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:15,120
The official Raspberry Pi drawing specifies a

8
00:00:14,972 --> 00:00:18,142
fifty-one by twenty-one millimetre board, one millimetre

9
00:00:17,994 --> 00:00:18,530
thick.

10
00:00:19,208 --> 00:00:21,212
The wireless antenna sits at the far

11
00:00:21,065 --> 00:00:21,625
edge.

12
00:00:22,302 --> 00:00:24,586
The datasheet says material must stay out

13
00:00:24,438 --> 00:00:25,776
of that antenna space.

14
00:00:26,703 --> 00:00:28,598
So this enclosure stops short of the

15
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:29,266
board end.

16
00:00:29,943 --> 00:00:32,215
The last eight millimetres project outside the

17
00:00:32,067 --> 00:00:32,737
case.

18
00:00:33,414 --> 00:00:35,407
Rounded walls and the floor are two

19
00:00:35,259 --> 00:00:38,259
point four millimetres thick, with editable dimensions.

20
00:00:39,186 --> 00:00:41,385
Two supports use the front mounting holes,

21
00:00:41,370 --> 00:00:43,921
with two provisional cradle rests farther back.

22
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:47,113
This green board is a simplified dimensional

23
00:00:46,965 --> 00:00:47,708
reference.

24
00:00:48,385 --> 00:00:51,227
Real component clearances and retention still need

25
00:00:51,079 --> 00:00:51,725
checking.

26
00:00:52,652 --> 00:00:55,154
The front allows a micro USB cable.

27
00:00:55,832 --> 00:00:58,043
Header openings and a control window leave

28
00:00:57,895 --> 00:00:59,147
access from above.

29
00:00:59,824 --> 00:01:02,266
The open tail keeps enclosure material away

30
00:01:02,118 --> 00:01:03,431
from the antenna edge.

31
00:01:04,108 --> 00:01:06,720
Wireless performance still needs a real test.

32
00:01:07,647 --> 00:01:09,749
Lift the lid to inspect the arrangement.

33
00:01:10,426 --> 00:01:12,528
Both case parts end before the antenna

34
00:01:12,380 --> 00:01:12,989
tail.

35
00:01:13,666 --> 00:01:15,659
Only the enclosure parts go into the

36
00:01:15,511 --> 00:01:17,164
manufacturing exports.

37
00:01:18,091 --> 00:01:19,817
The base and lid are valid solids

38
00:01:19,669 --> 00:01:21,455
and export as closed meshes.

39
00:01:22,133 --> 00:01:24,465
The next step is a physical prototype:

40
00:01:24,511 --> 00:01:27,390
check cable fit, board retention, heat and

41
00:01:27,242 --> 00:01:28,579
radio performance.

